Every live credential appears in public on every path that reaches finally. result.leftovers stays current per step and carries across phases through state. A killed process writes no result.json, and PLAN says so. No scenario killed a process.\n2. reviewBasis has the closed form, with its own qualifier case and scenario.\n3. change.review and change.merge are read in membershipUnchanged at every phase's boot, so in rehold they come before rehold-a.\n4. The corrections are in PLAN and collector.py:190, with Release reads naming the planner's read of the previous phase's receipt. The independent file's timing now runs at the start of work's checks, and a missing file records its row. PLAN also corrects your item and the agent's earlier report: an edit after admission fires setup-admission-predecessor-changed from recovery.mjs:158 first, not later-admission-changed.\n5. The independent token needs more than budget plus 15 s, 315 s. By arithmetic the planner has at most 585 s from mint to work. Nothing ran that window.\n\nPlease weigh these points. They go beyond your items and the rulings, or I found them while reading:\na. admit-later.mjs:15 accepts a refusal from the setup packet by class name, error.constructor.name === 'Stop', with the code held to a fixed-word pattern. This lets the real word surface. The agent chose it, and no ruling names it.\nb. After admission, the public word for a changed binding is operator-failed-private-detail-withheld, because the operator's catch doesn't know V15's Stop class. The agent saw the word beneath once in a scratch copy. Outside the collector no HALTED.json appears, and the next phase refuses too. I left this as it stands.\nc. independentRow echoes a tokenId with an id's shape that differs from token while the file is unchecked. A secret placed in that field would reach public output. The planner's channel writes the file, and shape is the only guard available.\nd. The operator's two new row words, not-refused and provider-not-refused-after-end, and stop.accepted in git.mjs are beyond your items. Without them, a 404 or 500 reads as accepted.\ne. Controls carried from V12 did not rerun: 10 scenario and 12 qualifier. The agent reports each broken string byte-present in V13, and I did not check that.\nf. Gaps in the controls: room-write-occurred has no control of its own, binding-changed-* has no broken copy because its check lives in the pinned V15 module, and the mint stop words, revoke-unknown and outcome-unknown appear only in qualifier cases.\ng. Nobody confirmed that the real room's admin holds change.review and change.merge. If not, rehold halts at boot with no original and no result.oldHolds.\nh. Per-phase times in PLAN are V12's. The rehearsal took 16 min 56 s beside other work, and I did not re-measure phases.\ni. reviewedSourceRoot and the two qualification roots exist on disk, which is an exception to absent names. assemble.py:83 and run-qualification.py:20 require the first, and the final qualification wrote the other two. The other five paths are absent.\n\nWhat did not run on V13: assemble.py, finalize-equivalence.mjs, review-check.mjs, any Worker request, any real provider status, and any private path. channel.py:279-290 and the fixed path are source readings. The gate did not run, because this Source is not in the repository.\n\nThe landed worktree is clean at 112eff12. Main is at 76cac675, and no Worker has been deployed since 112eff12: dap-demo health reads da13242c at 21:38 UTC. A deployment before J4 closes voids this Source.","body":{"conditions":"Review the complete Source at the two digests, the diff from V12, and the captures. An approval report has first line Verdict: APPROVED and the two digest lines each on its own line, with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Approval adopts the operator only. It releases nothing, and it is not J4 or S1 completion.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git